namespace fly.runtime

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Fly runtime — macOS (arm64/x86-64) backend, over libSystem (Rust-style FFI).
// Every OS interaction is an extern-C call to a libSystem symbol (macOS offers no
// stable raw syscalls). Ported from fly/runtime/platform/macOS/*.c.
//
// NOTE: written and compile-checked on Linux; NOT runtime-tested on macOS (no SDK
// available here). Differences from the Linux backend it mirrors:
//   • struct stat layout: st_mode @ 4 (u16), st_size @ 96 (i64)
//   • getdents → getdirentries64(fd, buf, size, *basep)
//   • CLOCK_MONOTONIC = 6 (Linux: 1)
//   • futex → __ulock_wait / __ulock_wake
//   • argv/env via _NSGetArgc / _NSGetArgv / _NSGetEnviron (no globals, no /proc)
//   • uname fields are 256 bytes each; exe path via _NSGetExecutablePath
// Linked against libSystem (see ToolChain macOS link path).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

// ── libSystem externs (empty body → pure `call @name`) ────────────────────────
